    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "2B ¼ ½ R2B < B . This would result in the probability Pða ¼ bj A; B 2 ½0; m Þ ¼ 6m3 3 j A Bj3, which scales cubically with A- B, and is therefore too small when A is close to B. It is unclear how to change the cubic scaling with ﬁnite communication. The following questions remain open: can multistage entanglement swapping be simulated with ﬁnite communication? Or can one prove, that above a certain value of N, an inﬁnite amount of communication is necessary?"
